# EXPERIMENTAL add-on (apply together with tb330fu.config): SukiSU-Ultra (a KernelSU fork) built into the kernel as drivers/kernelsu.
# STATUS: the kernel builds and scripts/kernel/crc-compare.py reports no changed export CRC, but the tablet was unreachable after booting it from boot_a; it was
# restored by flashing the previous boot image with fastboot.  The cause was not found.  Do not flash this without a way to capture an early boot log.
# It has to be built in: it calls kernel-internal functions that are not exported to modules, so a loadable module cannot be linked (modpost: undefined).
# Setup (not in this repo): link a checkout of SukiSU-Ultra's kernel/ directory as drivers/kernelsu, add obj-$(CONFIG_KSU) += kernelsu/ to drivers/Makefile
# and a `source` line for its Kconfig to drivers/Kconfig.  Change `default y` of config KSU in that Kconfig to `default n` first: build-kernel.sh runs
# olddefconfig before it merges a fragment, so a default-y option would otherwise be switched on in every build, this fragment or not.
CONFIG_KSU=y
